{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/2878-issues-with-the-geist-itself","id":2878,"title":"Issues with the \"Geist\" itself","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-04T13:59:06-08:00","id":2878,"title":"Issues with the \"Geist\" itself","content":"Well, i picked up my book again to run a longer series of sessions.<br /> Problem is: i read it twice and am still seriously troubled by the lack of information the corebook gives about the Geist.<br /> Especially during gameplay.<br /> While i get what the Geist is about, being a core of the game itself, it seems weakly fleshed out to me.<br /> I mean, WHEN does the Geist say WHAT to the SinEater? Can the SinEater talk to the Geist and does he get a response?<br /> Having a simple archetype is ok, but i just miss MORE information on the Geist in-game.<br /> Does a Geist scare his SinEater otherwise, if it feels neglected?<br /> <br /> Since Synergy ist not such a fast changing/fluid stat like Plasm for example, it\u00b4s very hard for me to flesh out the<br /> active side of the Geist from what i\u00b4ve read so far. So vague.....<br /> I think Orpheus (still a total different game) didn\u00b4t leave me with so many questions as Geist does.<br /> <br /> Couldn\u00b4t find more infos even in the Book of the dead.<br /> Have they added something in Geist 1.1 pdf?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/709-nihil","name":"Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T14:18:23-08:00","id":2895,"title":"","content":"They have not. However I am making slow but steady progress on my own rules update: The Geist Chronicles, in which there is lots of advice for what Geists are like and some simple rules for how they interact with Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T14:47:38-08:00","id":2918,"title":"","content":"To be fair, my reading was always 'Have it your way!'. We see a lot of example Geists - talkative ones, ones you never see or hear but <i>know</i> are there, ones who express themselves in weird, weird ways... And one of the sample adventures, Dem Bones, deals with a Geist who is <i>maddeningly annoying</i>... Guidelines would be nice, but ultimately I think, as with so much of Geist, you kinda have to customise it to fit.","signatur